test/check/error-names.sumspec:13:31:
   |
13 | unknown :: Todo -> Todo(Title(t))
   |                               ^
unknown name t; name a value with #t in the input or on the source side

test/check/error-names.sumspec:14:26:
   |
14 | twice Id#x :: Todo(Title#x) -> Todo
   |                          ^
x is named twice in this transition

test/check/error-names.sumspec:15:32:
   |
15 | onTarget :: Todo -> Todo(Title#t)
   |                                ^
a value is named only in the input or on the source side; on the target side, write the name alone: t

test/check/error-names.sumspec:16:25:
   |
16 | nameName Id#i :: Todo(i#j) -> Todo
   |                         ^
only a type pattern can be named; i already names a value

test/check/error-names.sumspec:17:58:
   |
17 | mismatch :: Todo(Mode.Editing(EditText#e)) -> Todo(Title(e))
   |                                                          ^
e has type EditText, but Text is expected here

test/check/error-names.sumspec:18:33:
   |
18 | primed Title#t :: Todo -> Todo(t')
   |                                 ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-names.sumspec:19:34:
   |
19 | notFactor Text#t :: Todo -> Todo(t)
   |                                  ^
t (of type Text) is not a factor of Todo (Id * Title * Mode)

